From 62f5c8e32e3aa3e38ee9fd5211084f42dfdd2534 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:05:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] uhf: add Phase 3 tag memory access and security
 operations (SRS sect4.10-4.11)

Extends the AIDL/Manager/Session/arbiter/service stack from Phase 1/2 with
readTagMemory, writeTagMemory, writeEpc, blockWrite, blockErase,
setVerifyWrites, killTag, lockTag, setAccessPassword and setKillPassword,
plus the new TagFilter Parcelable and the UHF_WRITE permission (its own
permission-group, since every dangerous permission in this manifest has
one).

What is and is not implemented with confidence here, deliberately kept
separate:

- Real, tested policy logic in UhfSessionArbiter: FR-MEM-06 word-range
  validation (including rejecting an odd-length data array instead of
  silently truncating it via integer division - caught by writing the
  test for it), FR-MEM-07 read-back write verification (on by default),
  FR-SEC-02 (an all-zero kill password is refused, not honoured),
  FR-SEC-04 (a permanent lock state requires explicit confirmation),
  FR-SEC-07 (every irreversible op is audited), and FR-STR-13 routing
  (all of these stop-apply-restart around an active stream, same as
  antenna/inventory ops). 26 new tests, 92/92 total passing.

- Wire payload encoding (buildTagOpPayload): explicitly UNVERIFIED,
  Confirm status pending OI-01 exactly like the SRS's own R1-pending
  command codes. This reader family's manual was not available when this
  was written, so the byte layout is a plausible, simple, clearly-isolated
  guess - the same posture as inventory()'s optional-triple encoding in
  the Phase 1 commit, not a new relaxation of standards. Read
  protection/EAS/vendor-extensions (sect4.12-4.14) are not implemented at
  all rather than guessed at with even less to go on than this section had.

UhfService: converts the framework TagFilter Parcelable to the arbiter's
framework-independent TagFilterSpec at the Binder boundary, matching the
pattern already established for UhfReaderInfo/InventoryParams. Cross-
checked by script, not by eye, exactly as the Phase 1/2 commits did:
every AIDL method (32) has exactly one BinderService override, every
UhfManager/UhfSession call matches the AIDL 1:1, every mArbiter.* call
matches an arbiter method 1:1. No mismatches found this round.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
